From fc59ff389b0621f3f86efb8aba5dd624388336cd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 23:41:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] phy: rockchip: inno-usb2: Fix the inverted suspend bit in
 rockchip_usb2phy_set_suspend()

rockchip_usb2phy_set_suspend() was split out of rockchip_usb2phy_power_on()
and rockchip_usb2phy_power_off() to hold the PHY suspend handling. The
original code cleared the phy_sus property to leave suspend
(property_enable(..., false) in power_on()) and set it to enter suspend
(property_enable(..., true) in power_off()). The helper passes
!do_suspend to property_enable(), so it now sets phy_sus when it is asked
to leave suspend and clears it when it is asked to suspend.

With the following change, which runs the helper from the 480 MHz clock's
prepare/unprepare on RK3588 and RK3576, every USB2 PHY there is put into
suspend as soon as its clock is prepared, and the UTMI clock towards the
controllers never runs. On an Orange Pi 5 (RK3588S) the xHCI behind the
Type-C port then stops counting MFINDEX, receives a single interrupt and
never sees the hubs of the connected dock: neither the USB 2.0 side nor
the USB 3.0 side, whose link reaches U0 but whose connect change the
controller cannot process. The EHCI controllers behind the other two
USB2 PHYs never interrupt either.

Pass do_suspend as is, so that the helper does what the code it replaced
did. With that, the Orange Pi 5 enumerates the dock's USB 2.0 and USB 3.0
hubs, the webcam and the SuperSpeed devices behind them again, the EHCI
controller sees its device, and they all survive a suspend/resume cycle.

Fixes: "phy: rockchip: inno-usb2: move suspend handling into new function" (v2 3/4, <20261001-phy-rockchip-inno-usb2-clock-fix-v2-3-e01bf509359e@collabora.com>)
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-usb2.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-usb2.c b/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-usb2.c
index 89281fc8d475..91748ba33460 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-usb2.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-usb2.c
@@ -338,7 +338,7 @@ static int rockchip_usb2phy_set_suspend(struct rockchip_usb2phy *rphy,
 {
 	int ret;
 
-	ret = property_enable(rphy->grf, &rport->port_cfg->phy_sus, !do_suspend);
+	ret = property_enable(rphy->grf, &rport->port_cfg->phy_sus, do_suspend);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
